  {
    "sha": "56f8faf0b2b692bcdbbd1fe0cae7a3af1e21436b",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDU2ZjhmYWYwYjJiNjkyYmNkYmJkMWZlMGNhZTdhM2FmMWUyMTQzNmI",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-22T19:47:44Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-22T19:47:44Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(gpu): deepen the twin spot check and give the timeout a kind\n\nTwo review items on PR #3532.\n\n1. The spot check probed only the centre cell of each sampled item, so a\n   chord that touches only the edge of its brick compared floor with floor.\n   It now probes the deepest claimed cell of each sampled item and 8 fixed\n   places across the lattice.\n\n2. The timeout latch read the text \"did not answer\" and missed the\n   read-back map wait that ends. CutKernel::run now returns a CutError with\n   a kind, and the latch fires on CutErrorKind::NoAnswer.\n\nPin tests: an_edge_only_chord_is_checked_at_its_deepest_cell,\na_wrong_texel_at_a_fixed_lattice_place_fails_the_spot_check,\na_map_wait_that_ends_latches_the_gpu_off,\ncut_gpu::tests::the_read_back_wait_that_ends_is_a_no_answer.\n\nFixes #2627\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>",
